s</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Tester</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The Na<sup>+</sup> transporter AtHKT1;1 controls retrieval of Na<sup>+</sup> from the xylem in <italic>Arabidopsis</italic></article-title><source>Plant, Cell and Environment</source><year>2007</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>497</fpage><lpage>507</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Deal</surname><given-names>KR</given-names></name><name><surname>Goyal</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Dvorak</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Arm location of <italic>Lophopyrum elongatum</italic> genes affecting K<sup>+</sup>/Na<sup>+</sup> selectivity under salt stress</article-title><source>Euphytica</source><year>1999</year><volume>108</volume><fpage>193</fpage><lpage>198</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Demidchik</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Davenport</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Tester</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nonselective cation channels in plants</article-title><source>Annual Review of Plant Biology</source><year>2002</year><volume>53</volume><fpage>67</fpage><lpage>107</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Epstein</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Norlyn</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><name><surname>Rush</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name><name><surname>Kingsbury</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name><name><surname>Kelley</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name><name><surname>Cunningham</surname><given-names>GA</given-names></name><name><surname>Wrona</surname><given-names>AF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Saline culture of crops: a genetic approach</article-title><source>Science</source><year>1980</year><volume>210</volume><fpage>399</fpage><lpage>404</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17837407</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Epstein</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Rains</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name><name><surname>Elzam</surname><given-names>OE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Resolution of dual mechanisms of potassium absorption by barley roots</article-title><source>Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences, USA</source><year>1963</year><volume>49</volume><fpage>684</fpage><lpage>692</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Essah</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>Davenport</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Tester</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Sodium influx and accumulation in <italic>Arabidopsis</italic></article-title><source>Plant Physiology</source><year>2003</year><volume>133</volume><fpage>307</fpage><lpage>318</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12970496</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Flowers</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Plants and salinity &#x02013; preface</article-title><source>Journal of Experimental Botany</source><year>2006</year><volume>57</volume><comment>(<italic>Special Issue: Plants and Salinity</italic>), iv</comment></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Flowers</surname><given-names>